+### Premium narration with VoiceStudio (optional)
+
+[VoiceStudio](https://github.com/debpalash/VoiceStudio) is a free, open-source voice app that runs on your own
+computer. With it open, `flow_narrate` with `engine: "voicestudio"` (or **Flow Studio → Voice → VoiceStudio ✦**) speaks
+in your own cloned or designed voices, in 646 languages, with personality presets, speed (0.5-2x), quality
+(draft, balanced, studio), a finishing effect (broadcast, cinematic, podcast, warm, bright, raw), a fixed seed for a
+repeatable read, an exact length to fit a shot, and whole scripts of up to 20,000 characters in one take. It also lets you
+pick any other speech engine you've installed in VoiceStudio, and that engine's built-in voices.
+
+1. Install it. Windows, in PowerShell: `irm https://voicestudio.sh/install | iex`. Mac, in Terminal:
+   `curl -fsSL https://voicestudio.sh/install | sh`. Or download it from its
+   [releases page](https://github.com/debpalash/VoiceStudio/releases/latest).
+2. Open it once and let it finish its first-run setup (it downloads its voice model, about 2.3 GB). It runs on any
+   computer, faster with a graphics card.
+3. Keep VoiceStudio open while you use Flow. **Flow Studio → Voice → VoiceStudio ✦** shows a green light when it's
+   ready, and lets you clone a voice from a recording or design one from a description.
+
+Flow talks to VoiceStudio at `http://127.0.0.1:3900`. Set `VOICESTUDIO_URL` to use one elsewhere (and
+`OMNIVOICE_API_KEY` if that one needs a key). Only clone a voice that is yours or that you have permission to use.
+
