+### Drama Studio: a whole micro-drama from a title and an idea
+
+**Flow Studio → Drama ✦** (or ask Claude: *"make a 60-second micro-drama called The CEO's Secret Twin about…"*) runs
+the whole pipeline and stops for your OK before anything that costs money:
+
+1. **Write**: script, characters, shots, dialogue, hook and cliffhanger
+2. **Cast**: a reference portrait of every character
+3. **Voices**: every line spoken, one distinct voice per character
+4. **Frames**: a still for each shot, with the characters kept on-model
+5. **Shots**: each frame animated, made long enough for its lines
+6. **Sound**: optional sound effects and music
+7. **Cut**: the finished vertical episode with captions
+
+You pick the generator for each step and can switch any time. Anything already made is kept, and any single portrait,
+line, frame or shot can be redone with a new prompt.
+
+| Step | Choices |
+|---|---|
+| Writer | Claude (Anthropic key), OpenAI, Gemini, or Claude in chat with no key |
+| Images | Flow (free), Gemini (Nano Banana), OpenAI (GPT Image), fal.ai (Nano Banana, FLUX 3), OpenRouter |
+| Video | Flow (your credits), fal.ai (Kling 4.0/3.0, Hailuo H3, Seedance 2.5/2.0, Wan 3.0, Gemini Omni), Google Gemini Omni Flash, Runway (Gen-4.5 and partner models), Kling, Higgsfield. OpenArt has no public API, so it can't be connected |
+| Voices | VoiceStudio (free, designs a voice per character), Google (free), this computer's voices, ElevenLabs, OpenAI |
+| Music and effects | ElevenLabs, or your own music file |
+
+Keys go in **Drama → Keys** and are saved only on your computer (`~/.flow-mcp/keys.json`). Claude can see which keys
+are saved, never the keys themselves. Every episode lives in `~/flow-mcp-out/Dramas/<title>/`, with the finished
+`<title>-episode.mp4` (plus a captioned copy) next to its cast, voices, frames and shots.
+
 ### Premium narration with VoiceStudio (optional)
 
 [VoiceStudio](https://github.com/debpalash/VoiceStudio) is a free, open-source voice app that runs on your own
